    {
      "cadence": "daily",
      "description": "15 min, Mon-Sat. Cards come from one source: what I built or\nbroke \u2014 every failure mode, every gotcha from ladder rungs and\nplatform Saturdays becomes a card.\n\nIn practice this is ONE sitting with the devops-ready cert deck\n(07:15-07:45 back-to-back) \u2014 two templates, one habit. (A shared\ncommon-task is specced in specs/common-tasks.md but not built.)\n\nAdd 3-5 new cards per day. No more. Crunch week? This survives.\n",
      "due": "today at 07:15",
      "fires": true,
      "id": "daily-anki",
      "labels": [
        "daily-ritual",
        "srs"
      ],
      "syllabus_key": "marketplace-builder",
      "title": "Anki review \u2014 build deck (15 min)"
    },
    {
      "cadence": "monthly",
      "description": "1st of the month: publish the ship log. Not a portfolio polish\nexercise \u2014 a factual list of what went LIVE this month on the\nbooking platform: endpoints shipped, infra stood up, gates passed,\nincidents survived.\n\nFormat:\n- What users (or test users) can do now that they couldn't last month\n- Exam gates passed this month\n- One thing that broke and what it taught\n- Link to the deployed thing\n\nPublish wherever the senior engineers and future employers will\nsee it (blog / LinkedIn / repo CHANGELOG \u2014 pick one and stick to it).\n",
      "due": "today at 09:30",
      "fires": true,
      "id": "monthly-ship-log",
      "labels": [
        "monthly-ritual",
        "ship-log"
      ],
      "syllabus_key": "marketplace-builder",
      "title": "Ship log \u2014 what went live in 2026-07"
