    {
      "cadence": "once-per-module",
      "description": "Concept: small sharp tools; parsing; table-driven tests; clean errors.\nPick ONE:\n  A. Expression calculator CLI \u2014 precedence, parentheses, good errors.\n  B. Markdown -> HTML converter \u2014 subset of MD, golden-file tests.\n  C. Flashcard drill CLI over your exported Anki decks \u2014 spaced\n     ordering, stats. (Consumer: your own daily review.)\nMust (all options): table-driven tests, garbage input handled,\nREADME, a consumer named in the ADR.\nADR question: how do you parse \u2014 and where's the seam between the\nCLI and the reusable core?\n",
      "due": "today at 20:00",
      "fires": true,
      "id": "rung-1",
      "labels": [
        "rung",
        "phase-1"
      ],
      "syllabus_key": "marketplace-builder",
      "title": "Rung 1: CLI craft & tests (~2 wk) \u2014 pick one of 3"
    },
